# Do Not Create Markdown Files

**NEVER** create `.md` files (documentation, README, changelog, etc.) unless the user explicitly asks for them.

## When Not to Create .md Files

- ❌ After implementing features (no CHANGELOG.md, FEATURES.md, etc.)
- ❌ For documentation (no API_DOCS.md, GUIDE.md, etc.)
- ❌ For configuration notes (no SETUP.md, CONFIG.md, etc.)
- ❌ For testing instructions (no TESTING.md, etc.)

## When .md Files Are OK

- ✅ User explicitly says "create a README" or "write documentation"
- ✅ Updating existing .md files that are already in the project
- ✅ User asks "can you document this?"

## What to Do Instead

Instead of creating documentation files:

- Add comments in code when necessary (but avoid obvious comments)
- Update existing documentation if it exists
- Explain verbally to the user in your response
- Wait for the user to ask for documentation

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Don't do this
// After implementing auth, create AUTH_SETUP.md to explain the changes

// ✅ GOOD: Just explain it to the user
// "I've implemented authentication with Better Auth. The session cookies
// are now configured for cross-subdomain support..."
```
